+---
+id: task-002-fix-coupon-after-volume-base-coupon-expiry-day-and-review-delivery-vat-report
+type: task
+title: "Fix coupon-after-volume base, coupon expiry day, and review delivery VAT report"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Fix coupon-after-volume base, coupon expiry day, and review delivery VAT report
+
+Three reports about the order service, each checked against the business rules in `README.md`.
+
+## 1. Coupon applied to the gross amount (finance)
+
+Twelve notebooks at €5.00 with a 10% coupon come to €48.00 of goods; finance expects €48.60.
+
+- Rule: a coupon applies to the order's subtotal after volume discounts. A fixed coupon never takes off
+  more than that subtotal. All discounts together stay within 50% of the gross amount.
+- Cause: `priceOrder` (`src/pricing.ts`) computes the coupon on `grossTotal`, so the 10% volume discount
+  on the 12 notebooks (€6.00) is counted twice: €6.00 volume + €6.00 coupon = €12.00 off instead of
+  €6.00 + €5.40 = €11.40.
+- Fix: compute the coupon on the subtotal after volume discounts; keep the 50% cap on the gross amount.
+
+## 2. Coupon refused on its last day (Luca, customer)
+
+AUTUMN was advertised as valid until 30 November; an order placed on 30 November was refused as expired.
+
+- Rule: a coupon is valid from its first day to its last day, both included.
+- Cause: `Coupons.redeemable` (`src/coupons.ts`) refuses when `date >= validUntil`, which excludes the last day.
+- Fix: refuse only when the date is after `validUntil`.
+
+## 3. VAT on delivery (Anna, customer) — no code change yet
+
+Her receipt shows €1.08 VAT on €4.90 of shipping, and she asks that delivery carry no VAT.
+
+- Rule in `README.md`: "Shipping is subject to VAT at the standard rate (22%), shown on its own line of
+  the receipt." The README states that when the code and the list disagree, the list is right.
+- The code does what the README says (`shippingVat` in `src/tax.ts`; `test/orders.test.ts` asserts
+  `shippingVatCents: 108`). Removing the VAT would change a documented business rule, which is not a
+  bug fix, so it is left unchanged here and raised for a decision by the business owner.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Cases 1 and 2 each have a test that fails before the fix and passes after it.
+- `npm test` passes in full.
+- Case 3: no change in behaviour; the open question is reported to the user.
